# Education expenditure and per-capita income: SSA vs Lower-middle-income aggregates (1975-2015)

**Data:** `data/worldbank_education_gdp.csv` — WDI-style wide export, 12 rows x 45 cols
(2 aggregate country groups x 6 series; 4 metadata cols + 41 year columns `1975 [YR1975]..2015 [YR2015]`).
**Scope:** correlational/associational only. No causal claim is made or supported.
**SEs:** Newey-West HAC, 4 lags (primary). PCSE and cluster-robust SEs are **not** viable: only N=2
aggregate panels (and SSA/LMC overlap).

## QC / metadata discrepancy (reported as required)
`datasets.json` describes the panel as "per capita GDP (in 2010 US$)" and "government expenditure on
education (% of total expenditure)". The file actually contains **GNI per capita (constant 2015 US$)**
`NY.GNP.PCAP.KD` and **Adjusted savings: education expenditure (% of GNI)** `NY.ADJ.AEDU.GN.ZS`.
All results below are therefore stated in **GNI per capita (2015 US$)** and **education expenditure as a
share of GNI**, not GDP per capita / share of government spending. Blanks -> NaN, no imputation, no
external data; 0 non-numeric cells; 128/492 cells (26%) blank.

