## Step A - descriptive trends 1975-2015
Education expenditure (% of GNI), decade means: SSA 4.33 / 4.35 / **5.15** / 3.93 / 3.42
(1970s..2010s); LMC 3.51 / 3.47 / 3.71 / 3.52 / 3.19. SSA peak **6.10% (1997)**, then a fall to
3.15% (2015); LMC peak 3.87% (1999) -> 3.06% (2015). **SSA spent ~0.80pp of GNI more than LMC on
average across the whole period (4.30 vs 3.50).**
GNI/capita: LMC 881 (1975) -> 1965 (2015), 2.03%/yr. SSA only 1555 (2011) -> 1634 (2015), 1.25%/yr.
Enrolment (GER): SSA primary 60.6 -> 97.0 (+36.4pp); SSA secondary 14.8 -> 43.4 (+28.6pp);
LMC primary 79.1 -> 101.8; LMC secondary 27.8 -> 64.5 (+36.7pp). SSA's expansion is heavily
primary-weighted and its secondary GER in 2015 (43) is still ~21pp below LMC's.
Levels-vs-changes reversal (LMC, n=41/40): r(ln Y, edu) = **-0.434**; r(growth, edu level) = -0.180;
r(growth, Δ edu) = **+0.191**. Detrended (linear) residual correlation ln Y vs edu = **-0.551**.

